{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter's Job Interview", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "No News Is Good News", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information on instructions about basic activities and safety at work.  ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Giving and Responding to Bad News", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are different ways to give and respond to bad news.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Examples</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Giving bad news </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I've got some bad news for you! <br />I regret to inform you that ... <br />I'm sorry but ... <br />Unfortunately, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Responding to bad news </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Oh no/dear! <br />I can't believe it! <br />I'm sorry to hear that ... <br />That's unfortunate/awful! <br />I know how you must be feeling!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "news ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "new information ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have some bad news!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you give or respond to bad news.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to stress", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to feel very worried  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Waiting for a call is stressing me out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take your mind off things", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend time away from something  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's go to the park. It helps to take your mind off things.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to come up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to appear ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My e-mails aren't coming up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to regret ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say that you are sorry for something. ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I regret to inform you that it is raining outside.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn2le08ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Simple Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Use the Present Simple to talk about facts and usual actions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "To form the negative, use do/does not  before the verb. </br>Do not add s to the verb when used with he, she, it.</br> Pay attention to the short form <span class=\"italic\">don't</span>. It's used in talking.</br></br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To form a yes/no question, use do/does and change the word order like this:         \tDo/Does + subject + verb </br>Do not add s to the verb with he, she, it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I really want this job!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Don't worry.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a short dialogue about bad news (6-8 lines).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Your friend's phone is not working. They share the bad news with you.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Respond to their bad news.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use simple connectors like <span class=\"italic\">and</span>, <span class=\"italic\">or</span>, <span class=\"italic\">but</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice your di